Title: Open the parent process with SYNCHRONIZE in the relauncher before Vista
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

app.relaunch() starts a helper process, electron.exe --type=relauncher, which
waits for the application that started it to exit and then starts it again.
To wait, it opens its parent with PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS.

That constant is not one value. Before the Vista SDK it was
STANDARD_RIGHTS_REQUIRED | SYNCHRONIZE | 0xFFF; since, it ends in 0xFFFF,
for the process rights Vista added. Windows XP refuses an access mask
containing bits it does not define, so there OpenProcess fails with
ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED. Nothing checks the handle: WaitForSingleObject is given
null, fails immediately, and the helper goes straight on to start the
application -- while the old instance is still shutting down, with its
profile directory and whatever files it keeps still open.

The wait needs SYNCHRONIZE and nothing else, so that is what is asked for
before Vista. From Vista on the request is left as upstream has it.

diff --git a/electron/shell/browser/relauncher_win.cc b/electron/shell/browser/relauncher_win.cc
--- a/electron/shell/browser/relauncher_win.cc
+++ b/electron/shell/browser/relauncher_win.cc
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include "base/strings/strcat_win.h"
 #include "base/strings/string_number_conversions_win.h"
 #include "base/win/scoped_handle.h"
+#include "base/win/windows_version.h"
 #include "sandbox/win/src/nt_internals.h"
 #include "sandbox/win/src/win_utils.h"
 #include "shell/common/command_line_util_win.h"
@@ -48,7 +49,15 @@
     return nullptr;
   }
 
-  return ::OpenProcess(PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS, TRUE, ppid);
+  // Before Vista, SYNCHRONIZE, which is all the wait on this handle needs.
+  // PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS grew in the Vista SDK, and Windows XP refuses an access
+  // mask with bits it does not define: the open fails with
+  // ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED, the wait returns at once, and the application is
+  // started again while the old instance is still shutting down.
+  const DWORD access = base::win::GetVersion() < base::win::Version::VISTA
+                           ? SYNCHRONIZE
+                           : PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS;
+  return ::OpenProcess(access, TRUE, ppid);
 }
 
 }  // namespace
